Ask the user for the path to a specific CLI tool when a call fails with `command not found` or similar.

`rg`, `es`, `open`, and nu's `ls`/`find` via this tool can reach anywhere on the filesystem; shell respect neither `gitignore` nor `.zed/settings.json`.
{{#if is_windows}}
- Never create or redirect to a file named `nul`, `con`, `prn`, `aux`, `com1`-`com9`, or `lpt1`-`lpt9` -- these are Windows reserved names.
- In `nu`, `\` inside a double-quoted string is an escape character, you may prefer single-quoted string e.g. `'C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin'` or raw string e.g. `r#'C:\Program Files\Git\usr\bin'#`(delimiter hash characters >= 1) for static args.
- Use `es` (Everything Search) instead of `ls` for filename/path search -- it reaches anywhere, fast. Reach for `es` first when you need to search a repo not in `$env.PWD`.
{{/if}}

Never hardcode a long `sleep <n>`. Poll with a bounded 1s-interval loop instead:
```nu
let limit = 240; for i in 1..$limit { if (netstat -ano | lines | any {|l| $l =~ "<port>.*LISTENING" }) { print $"Port <port> listening after ($i)s"; break }; sleep 1sec }
```
